        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The postgres database was nearly at its connection limit (396/400).\n- Logs showed that the reporting-job service was holding onto 340 connections, likely due to a connection leak (\"connections not returned after query timeout\").\n- This caused the checkout service to fail with \"too many clients\" errors.\n\nRemediation:\n- I restarted the reporting-job service to clear the leaked connections.\n- After the restart, postgres connections dropped from 396 to 61, and checkout error rates returned to near zero.\n\nSummary:\nA connection leak in reporting-job exhausted postgres connections, impacting checkout. Restarting reporting-job resolved the issue and restored normal operation.",
